<h2>Where should the filters sit on the activity page?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">Event type plus date range. All three use components from 02 Components; they differ in how much space the filters take and how visible the active filters are.</p>

<style>
  .wf { font-size: 13px; }
  .wf .row { display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: flex-end; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .wf .fs { border: 1px dashed #999; padding: 6px 8px; border-radius: 4px; }
  .wf .fs b { display: block; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .wf .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, auto); gap: 2px 14px; }
  .wf .field span { display: block; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 2px; }
  .wf .box { border: 1px solid #999; padding: 3px 6px; border-radius: 4px; min-width: 90px; display: inline-block; }
  .wf .tag { border: 1px solid #999; border-radius: 12px; padding: 1px 8px; display: inline-block; margin-right: 4px; }
  .wf .tag.acc { border-color: #3b82f6; }
  .wf .meta { color: #666; margin: 6px 0; }
  .wf table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
  .wf td, .wf th { border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 3px 4px; text-align: left; }
  .wf .pop { border: 1px solid #999; border-radius: 6px; padding: 8px; box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.15); width: 300px; margin: 4px 0 8px; }
</style>

<div class="options">
  <div class="option" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">A</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Always-visible filter panel</h3>
      <div class="mockup"><div class="mockup-body wf">
        <div class="row">
          <div class="fs"><b>Event type</b>
            <div class="grid">
              <label>☐ Sign-in</label><label>☑ Sign-in failed</label><label>☐ Sign-out</label>
              <label>☐ Session expired</label><label>☐ Password changed</label><label>☐ Two-factor enabled</label>
              <label>☐ Email change requested</label><label>☐ Settings updated</label><label>☐ API token used</label>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <div class="field"><span>Period</span><div class="box">Last 30 days ▾</div></div>
          <div class="field"><span>From</span><div class="box">Sep 2, 2026 📅</div></div>
          <div class="field"><span>To</span><div class="box">Oct 2, 2026 📅</div></div>
          <button class="mock-button">Clear filters</button>
        </div>
        <div class="meta">Showing 8 of 48 events</div>
        <table><tr><th>When</th><th>Event</th><th>Device</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Sep 27, 2026, 5:03 PM</td><td>Sign-in failed</td><td>Firefox on Windows</td></tr></table>
      </div></div>
      <p>Everything visible at once, nothing to open. Takes about 5 lines above the table; checkbox list is the 03 Forms pattern for "several independent options".</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">B</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>"Filter" button opens a popover; active filters shown as tags</h3>
      <div class="mockup"><div class="mockup-body wf">
        <div class="row"><button class="mock-button">Filter ▾</button>
          <span class="tag acc">Sign-in failed ✕</span><span class="tag">Last 30 days ✕</span>
          <a href="#" onclick="return false">Clear filters</a></div>
        <div class="pop"><b>Event type</b> (same 9 checkboxes)<br><br><b>Period</b> / From / To</div>
        <div class="meta">Showing 8 of 48 events</div>
        <table><tr><th>When</th><th>Event</th><th>Device</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Sep 27, 2026, 5:03 PM</td><td>Sign-in failed</td><td>Firefox on Windows</td></tr></table>
      </div></div>
      <p>Table starts almost at the top. One extra click to change filters; more JS (popover focus, Escape, outside click) and more review surface.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">C</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Compact single row: type combobox with chips + dates</h3>
      <div class="mockup"><div class="mockup-body wf">
        <div class="row">
          <div class="field"><span>Event type</span><div class="box" style="min-width:200px"><span class="tag">Sign-in failed ✕</span> type to add…</div></div>
          <div class="field"><span>Period</span><div class="box">Last 30 days ▾</div></div>
          <div class="field"><span>From</span><div class="box">Sep 2 📅</div></div>
          <div class="field"><span>To</span><div class="box">Oct 2 📅</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="meta">Showing 8 of 48 events · <a href="#" onclick="return false">Clear filters</a></div>
        <table><tr><th>When</th><th>Event</th><th>Device</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Sep 27, 2026, 5:03 PM</td><td>Sign-in failed</td><td>Firefox on Windows</td></tr></table>
      </div></div>
      <p>One row of controls. The nine types are hidden behind typing/opening, and a combobox is the most custom JS of the three for only nine options.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
